<section class="clearwater-section">
  <div class="clearwater-container clearwater-container--narrow">
    <div class="clearwater-prose">
      <h2>The promise.</h2>
      <p>When Sam started Clearwater in 1997, he made a list of the things he hated about the plumbing companies he'd worked for. It was a long list. The short version became our promise:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A real human answers the phone during business hours. No phone trees, no callbacks.</li>
        <li>Every price is known before work starts. Flat-rate, in writing.</li>
        <li>The jobsite is cleaner when we leave than when we arrived. Always.</li>
        <li>If a repair fails inside a year, we come back on our dime. No paperwork, no arguments.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Twenty-eight years and 7,800 jobs later, we've never changed it.</p>

      <h2>The three generations.</h2>
      <h3>Sam Kovac &middot; Founder, semi-retired</h3>
      <p>Colorado master plumber, founded Clearwater in 1997 after 15 years as a service tech with a large SLC outfit. Sam still comes into the shop Tuesday and Thursday mornings to "make sure the boy is doing it right." He's usually right that we are.</p>

      <h3>Mike Kovac &middot; Owner, master plumber</h3>
      <p>Grew up in the truck. Earned his master license in 2012. Took over day-to-day operations from Sam in 2018. Runs the big jobs himself — repipes, commercial remodels, and anything his estimators flagged as "complicated." Answers the phone on weekends.</p>

      <h3>Tess Kovac &middot; Office manager</h3>
      <p>Joined the family in 2013 and the business in 2015. Runs dispatch, billing, and every piece of the customer experience that isn't under a sink. When you call Clearwater during business hours, chances are high you're talking to Tess.</p>

      <h2>The crew.</h2>
      <p>Six licensed plumbers — one master, four journeymen, one apprentice. All W-2, all drug-tested, all background-checked. No subcontractors wearing Clearwater shirts. The person on your roof is the person who works here.</p>

      <h2>What we won't do.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Upsell unnecessary fixtures or equipment when the repair you called about is a simple one.</li>
        <li>Push a new water heater when yours has a $20 thermocouple failure.</li>
        <li>Quote a repair without putting eyes on the problem, unless you insist.</li>
        <li>Work without a permit where code requires one. Even when the inspector's a hassle.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to know if we're a fit.</h2>
      <p>If you want the cheapest option in the Valley, we're not it. Our flat rates are priced so we can pay our plumbers a living wage, carry real insurance, and warranty our work for a year. That adds up to about 10–15% over the bottom of the market.</p>
      <p>What you get in exchange is a crew that doesn't turn over every six months, a shop that's been here 28 years, and a phone that someone actually answers. Most of our customers say it's worth it. Many of them are second-generation — their parents called Clearwater in the '90s and now they do too.</p>
